#: ../../../SphinxQuickstartTemplate.md:107
msgid "Code Blocks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SphinxQuickstartTemplate.md:109
msgid "You can make blocks of code like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SphinxQuickstartTemplate.md:117
msgid ""
"For a shell session, use a `console` code block (some existing docs use "
"`bash`):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SphinxQuickstartTemplate.md:125
msgid "If you need to show LLVM IR, use the `llvm` code block."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SphinxQuickstartTemplate.md:134
msgid ""
"Some other common code blocks you might need are `c`, `objc`, `make`, and "
"`cmake`. If you need something beyond that, you can look at the [full list] "
"of supported code blocks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SphinxQuickstartTemplate.md:140
msgid ""
"However, don't waste time fiddling with syntax highlighting when you could "
"be adding meaningful content. When in doubt, show preformatted text without "
"any syntax highlighting like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SphinxQuickstartTemplate.md:163
msgid "Sphinx Directives"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SphinxQuickstartTemplate.md:165
msgid ""
"Sphinx directives that contain rich, formatted Markdown content should use "
"[colon fences][colon_fence] instead of backtick fences. This keeps directive "
"containers visually distinct from code blocks while still allowing normal "
"Markdown markup inside the directive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SphinxQuickstartTemplate.md:171
msgid ""
"Use colon fences for rich directives such as `{note}`, `{warning}`, `{option}"
"`, and similar content blocks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SphinxQuickstartTemplate.md:175
msgid "Prefer triple backtick fences for code regions and literal examples:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SphinxQuickstartTemplate.md:181
msgid ""
"Keep `{eval-rst}` blocks fenced with backticks, because their contents are "
"reStructuredText rather than Markdown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SphinxQuickstartTemplate.md:186
msgid "Generating the documentation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SphinxQuickstartTemplate.md:188
msgid ""
"You can generate the HTML documentation from the sources locally if you want "
"to see what they would look like. In addition to the normal [build tools]"
"(project:GettingStarted.md) you need to install [Sphinx] and the necessary "
"extensions using the following command inside the `llvm-project` checkout:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SphinxQuickstartTemplate.md:198
msgid ""
"Then run cmake to build the documentation inside the `llvm-project` checkout:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SphinxQuickstartTemplate.md:207
msgid ""
"In case you already have the Cmake build set up and want to reuse that, just "
"set the CMake variable `LLVM_ENABLE_SPHINX=On`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SphinxQuickstartTemplate.md:210
msgid ""
"After that you find the generated documentation in `build/docs/html` folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SphinxQuickstartTemplate.md:215
msgid "Markdown migration guidelines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SphinxQuickstartTemplate.md:217
msgid "These are some goals to keep in mind during a migration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SphinxQuickstartTemplate.md:219
msgid ""
"Optimize for review: Decompose the migration into mechanical steps that are "
"easy to review and validate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SphinxQuickstartTemplate.md:220
msgid ""
"Enable source code archaelogy: Expect future readers to want to know when "
"documentation policy changed, so keep your changes mechanical to make that "
"easy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SphinxQuickstartTemplate.md:221
msgid ""
"Minimize conflicts: LLVM is a big community of many developers with lots of "
"development branches and downstreams. Make conflict resolution easy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SphinxQuickstartTemplate.md:223
msgid ""
"For that reason, it's helpful to create 2-3 {ref}`stacked pull requests "
"<stacked_pull_requests>`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SphinxQuickstartTemplate.md:225
msgid ""
"Rename `.rst` -> `.md` and update cross-references. This will presumably "
"break the docs build, but to follow the one-PR-per-commit policy, it must be "
"its own PR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SphinxQuickstartTemplate.md:226
msgid ""
"Mechanically update reST conventions to markdown (\\`\\` -> \\`). Avoid "
"unnecessary reflow. This means you should avoid tools like pandoc, which "
"reflow paragraphs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SphinxQuickstartTemplate.md:227
msgid ""
"(optional) Reflow text in line with current project policy. You don't have "
"to do this, but if you feel the need to, make it a separate step. This can "
"be resequenced as step 1. Separating out the text reflow step makes it easy "
"to review and follow blame."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../SphinxQuickstartTemplate.md:229
msgid ""
"Don't rely too heavily on automated error checking to catch any "
"documentation bugs. If you are migrating a long doc, you are reponsible for "
"building the docs locally and validating the rendering yourself using the "
"steps above."
msgstr ""
